{
	"name": "Batch presentations with Presentations.AI Get Status",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Start several presentations, then check them later\n\n### How it works\nThis workflow starts one presentation per topic without waiting, so the batch doesn't hold a single long request. Each presentation gets a request ID. After a 2-minute pause, **Check the presentation status** asks Presentations.AI how each one is doing and downloads the file when it's ready. **Route by status** sends finished presentations to **Collect the file** and stops the workflow if one failed. Anything still running goes back to **Wait 2 minutes** and is checked again.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node package `@presentations-ai/n8n-nodes-presentations-ai` (tested with version 0.3.2). Follow [n8n's guide to installing verified community nodes](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/verified-install/).\n2. Create an API key at [api.presentations.ai](https://api.presentations.ai/#/apikeys) with the **Deck automation** preset, then create a **Presentations.AI API** credential with it and select it on the Presentations.AI node. Presentations.AI charges credits per slide.\n3. Click **Execute workflow**. It uses three example topics and creates three presentations, so it uses credits.\n\n### Customization\nReplace **List example topics** with your own source, such as a spreadsheet or database, and replace **Collect the file** with an upload to Drive or Slack. The loop stops after about 15 checks (about 30 minutes) through **Stop when it takes too long**, so a presentation that never finishes can't loop forever; change the number in **Route by status**. A failure stops the whole run. To keep the other presentations going, route **FAILED** to a notification instead of the stop node. Add **Slide Count**, **Brand Kit** or **Export Format** under the create node.",
				"width": 560,
				"height": 780,
				"color": 1
			},
			"id": "a4b38d3b-d4f2-536a-99e1-b82c216a2e75",
			"name": "Overview",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-640,
				-220
			]
		},
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## 1. Start the presentations\nCreate From Topic with **Wait for Completion** off returns right away with `request_id` and status.",
				"width": 640,
				"height": 320,
				"color": 7
			},
			"id": "74104c7f-a830-524b-8eeb-33dcb0df66c9",
